        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Concrete resurfacer is a thin coat of polymer-modified cement that bonds to an old slab and gives it a new wearing surface. It does not fix cracks, heaving or a failed base, and it will not stick to dirty, sealed or crumbling concrete. Put it on a sound, scrubbed slab at the right thickness and it can add years of good looks for a weekend of work. Put it anywhere else and it peels in the first winter.
        </p>

