          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best concrete resurfacer for most people is Quikrete Re-Cap: forgiving to mix, rated from a feather edge to half an inch, and ready for cars in about a day. Choose Rapid Set NewCrete when downtime matters, Sakrete Flo-Coat as a like-for-like alternative, and use the patchers and Cement All for the deep repairs a resurfacer should never be asked to fill.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The bag is the easy part. A resurfacer only lasts on sound concrete that has been stripped of sealer, pressure washed, patched and dampened, with every control joint preserved and every moving crack sealed with something flexible. Do the prep and it will make an old slab look new for years; skip it and no product on this list will save you.
